## THE QUESTION (read WHOLE first)
KS-2276 on the Secuura Linear board (read its description whole; its fix shape is "one control cell"). At develop 2ad55cec the route line is `Blockchain/Dev/services/vc-issuer/src/routes/presentations.ts` line 388: `domainValid: !domain || proof?.domain === domain,` (its twin at 387 is `challengeValid: !challenge || proof?.challenge === challenge`). The test file `ks625-...test.ts` (150 lines) pins `challengeValid` both ways (cell P6, a mismatched challenge: `challengeValid` false) but pins `domainValid` one way only: cell P1 expects `domainValid: true` for the matching domain. Cells P2, P3, P4 assert `proofValid` only, P5 `allCredentialsValid` only, P7 `credentialResults` and `all` only. So `domainValid: true` as a constant survives all seven cells. The ticket's fix: sign a presentation with one domain, verify with a different one, expect `domainValid` false (and, naturally, `verified` false: it is false for every presentation until the holder-signature check exists, so `verified` alone proves nothing: the cell must assert `checks.domainValid`).
**Also in the ticket (not built unless the ANSWER says so):** the older ks444 cell "an OBJECT proof reaches the verification logic" now guards only its 200-not-400 boundary: read it, report, do not widen.

